{"id":"js-arrays-metodo-slice","title":"JS - Arrays - Método slice","topic":"javascript","topicLabel":"JavaScript","tags":["aprendizaje","javascript","arrays"],"course":null,"headings":[{"depth":2,"text":"¿Qué es?","id":"que-es"},{"depth":3,"text":"Parámetros:","id":"parametros"},{"depth":2,"text":"¿Cómo se escribe? (Sintaxis)","id":"como-se-escribe-sintaxis"},{"depth":3,"text":"1. Extraer una porción intermedia","id":"1-extraer-una-porcion-intermedia"},{"depth":3,"text":"2. Extraer desde una posición hasta el final","id":"2-extraer-desde-una-posicion-hasta-el-final"},{"depth":3,"text":"3. Crear una copia idéntica del array","id":"3-crear-una-copia-identica-del-array"},{"depth":3,"text":"4. Índices negativos","id":"4-indices-negativos"}],"readingMins":1,"codeBlocks":4,"words":215,"backlinks":[{"id":"sesion-28-17-06-26","title":"Sesion_28_17.06.26","topicLabel":"UI/UX","session":28}],"html":"<h2 id=\"que-es\" class=\"note__h note__h--2\">¿Qué es?</h2><p>El método <code>slice()</code> (rebanar o cortar) se utiliza para extraer una sección o porción de un array y devolverla dentro de un <strong>nuevo array</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Regla de oro</strong>: <code>slice()</code> <strong>no modifica el array original</strong> (es un método no mutador). Devuelve una copia superficial (shallow copy) de los elementos seleccionados.</p>\n<h3 id=\"parametros\" class=\"note__h\">Parámetros:</h3><p><code>array.slice(inicio, fin)</code></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>inicio</code></strong>: Índice base cero donde empezará la extracción. Si es negativo, indica un desplazamiento desde el final del array.</li>\n<li><strong><code>fin</code></strong> (opcional): Índice base cero <em>antes</em> del cual terminar la extracción. <strong>No se incluye el elemento en esta posición</strong>. Si se omite, extraerá hasta el final del array. Si es negativo, indica un desplazamiento desde el final del array.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"como-se-escribe-sintaxis\" class=\"note__h note__h--2\">¿Cómo se escribe? (Sintaxis)</h2><h3 id=\"1-extraer-una-porcion-intermedia\" class=\"note__h\">1. Extraer una porción intermedia</h3><div class=\"codeblock\"><div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">javascript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>copiar</button></div><pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"hljs\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">let</span> numeros = [<span class=\"hljs-number\">10</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">20</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">30</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">40</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">50</span>];\n\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">// Extrae desde el índice 1 hasta el índice 4 (no incluido)</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">let</span> parte = numeros.<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">slice</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span>);\n\n<span class=\"hljs-variable language_\">console</span>.<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">log</span>(parte);   <span class=\"hljs-comment\">// [20, 30, 40]</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-variable language_\">console</span>.<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">log</span>(numeros); <span class=\"hljs-comment\">// [10, 20, 30, 40, 50] (El original sigue intacto)</span></code></pre></div><h3 id=\"2-extraer-desde-una-posicion-hasta-el-final\" class=\"note__h\">2. Extraer desde una posición hasta el final</h3><div class=\"codeblock\"><div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">javascript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>copiar</button></div><pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"hljs\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">let</span> nombres = [<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;Ana&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;Luis&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;Marta&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;Juan&quot;</span>];\n\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">// Omitimos el segundo parámetro para ir hasta el final</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">let</span> ultimos = nombres.<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">slice</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>);\n\n<span class=\"hljs-variable language_\">console</span>.<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">log</span>(ultimos); <span class=\"hljs-comment\">// [&quot;Marta&quot;, &quot;Juan&quot;]</span></code></pre></div><h3 id=\"3-crear-una-copia-identica-del-array\" class=\"note__h\">3. Crear una copia idéntica del array</h3><p>Si llamamos a <code>slice()</code> sin argumentos, clona el array por completo. Esto es útil para poder ordenar o modificar una lista sin alterar la original.</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\"><div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">javascript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>copiar</button></div><pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"hljs\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">let</span> original = [<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;A&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;B&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;C&quot;</span>];\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">let</span> copia = original.<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">slice</span>();\n\ncopia.<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">push</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;D&quot;</span>);\n\n<span class=\"hljs-variable language_\">console</span>.<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">log</span>(original); <span class=\"hljs-comment\">// [&quot;A&quot;, &quot;B&quot;, &quot;C&quot;] (Original intacto)</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-variable language_\">console</span>.<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">log</span>(copia);    <span class=\"hljs-comment\">// [&quot;A&quot;, &quot;B&quot;, &quot;C&quot;, &quot;D&quot;]</span></code></pre></div><h3 id=\"4-indices-negativos\" class=\"note__h\">4. Índices negativos</h3><div class=\"codeblock\"><div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">javascript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>copiar</button></div><pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"hljs\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">let</span> frutas = [<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;manzana&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;pera&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;plátano&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;melón&quot;</span>];\n\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">// Obtiene los 2 últimos elementos del array</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">let</span> ultimasDos = frutas.<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">slice</span>(-<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>);\n\n<span class=\"hljs-variable language_\">console</span>.<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">log</span>(ultimasDos); <span class=\"hljs-comment\">// [&quot;plátano&quot;, &quot;melón&quot;]</span></code></pre></div>"}